function bilayerSvg(clickable=true){let heads='',tails='',chol='',gchain='';for(let i=0;i<23;i++){let x=65+i*28; heads+=`<circle cx="${x}" cy="153" r="12" fill="#b19deb" stroke="#e7dcff" stroke-width="2"/><circle cx="${x}" cy="286" r="12" fill="#b19deb" stroke="#e7dcff" stroke-width="2"/>`;tails+=`<path d="M${x-5} 166 q-11 27 0 54 q11 27 0 53 M${x+5} 166 q11 26 0 54 q-11 28 0 53" stroke="#e9b75b" stroke-width="4" fill="none" opacity=".95"/>`}
 for(let i=0;i<4;i++)chol+=`<g transform="translate(${120+i*150} 205)" fill="#ffd66f" stroke="#bb8434" stroke-width="2"><polygon points="0,-19 15,-10 15,9 0,18 -15,9 -15,-10"/><polygon points="0,18 14,25 9,43 -7,45 -15,30"/></g>`;
 const click=(part)=>clickable?`onclick="selectPart('${part}')" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-label="${part}"`:'', hot=(id)=>`class="hot" ${click(id)}`;
 return `<svg class="svg-bilayer" role="img" aria-label="Interactive cell membrane diagram" viewBox="0 0 780 410" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><defs><linearGradient id="protg" x1="0" x2="1"><stop stop-color="#45c4d6"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#2879ba"/></linearGradient><linearGradient id="protp" x1="0" x2="1"><stop stop-color="#b785d5"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#6a4cc0"/></linearGradient></defs><rect width="780" height="410" rx="22" fill="#f4faff"/><text x="29" y="40" font-size="19" font-weight="800" fill="#56809a">OUTSIDE CELL</text><text x="29" y="366" font-size="19" font-weight="800" fill="#56809a">CYTOPLASM</text><g ${hot('Phospholipid bilayer')}>${tails}${heads}</g><g ${hot('Cholesterol')}>${chol}</g><g ${hot('Channel protein')}><path d="M307 150 C280 161 279 187 291 216 C280 249 291 279 308 290 L325 290 L327 167 L340 167 L343 291 L359 291 C382 268 367 241 371 218 C382 183 374 160 357 150 L340 168 L328 167 Z" fill="url(#protg)" stroke="#2668ae" stroke-width="3"/><path d="M333 170 L333 275" stroke="#e7fdff" stroke-width="10" stroke-linecap="round"/></g><g ${hot('Carrier protein')}><path d="M448 147 Q416 159 421 191 Q438 220 429 243 Q411 273 452 288 Q471 287 474 251 Q487 228 488 202 Q497 169 477 149 L468 187 L453 187 Z" fill="url(#protp)" stroke="#7653bd" stroke-width="3"/></g><g ${hot('Glycoprotein')}><ellipse cx="204" cy="148" rx="31" ry="41" fill="#b387d2" stroke="#8150b9" stroke-width="3"/><path d="M204 111 L204 79 M204 83 L184 64 M204 81 L224 63 M184 65 L171 48 M224 64 L238 47" fill="none" stroke="#239c7b" stroke-width="10" stroke-linecap="round"/></g><g ${hot('Glycolipid')}><path d="M561 143 L559 113 L543 99 M559 112 L574 93" stroke="#28ad91" stroke-width="9" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round"/><circle cx="543" cy="97" r="8" fill="#20b59b"/><circle cx="575" cy="93" r="8" fill="#20b59b"/></g><g ${hot('Extrinsic protein')}><ellipse cx="576" cy="317" rx="50" ry="20" fill="#759bd8" stroke="#5177b5" stroke-width="3"/></g><g ${hot('Hydrophilic head')}><circle cx="694" cy="153" r="16" fill="#c2aaff" stroke="#7656c1" stroke-width="4"/></g><g ${hot('Hydrophobic tails')}><path d="M703 180 q-14 28 0 55 q9 17 0 33 M717 180 q14 28 0 55 q-9 17 0 33" stroke="#df9657" stroke-width="7" fill="none"/></g><text x="390" y="398" font-size="13" text-anchor="middle" fill="#66869e">Tap a component to identify it</text></svg>`}
const COMPONENTS={
 'Phospholipid bilayer':'The hydrophilic phosphate heads face water; the hydrophobic tails form a central barrier to many polar/charged molecules.',
 'Hydrophilic head':'Polar phosphate-containing end that interacts with water outside and inside the cell.',
 'Hydrophobic tails':'Non-polar fatty-acid chains; they point inward to avoid water.',
 'Channel protein':'Intrinsic protein forming a hydrophilic passage for selected ions or molecules down their gradient.',
 'Carrier protein':'Intrinsic protein that binds specific molecules and changes shape; carriers support facilitated diffusion or active transport.',
 'Cholesterol':'Regulates membrane fluidity and stability; found between many animal-cell phospholipids.',
 'Glycoprotein':'Carbohydrate-bearing protein at the cell surface; recognition, signalling and adhesion.',
 'Glycolipid':'Carbohydrate-bearing lipid; may act as a cell-recognition marker.',
 'Extrinsic protein':'A peripheral protein attached to one surface of the membrane rather than spanning the bilayer.'
};
function selectPart(name){state.selectedPart=name;const el=$('#partDetail');if(el)el.innerHTML=`<div class="eyebrow">SELECTED STRUCTURE</div><h3>${esc(name)}</h3><p>${COMPONENTS[name]}</p>`;}
window.selectPart=selectPart;
function lesson(id){const l=LESSONS.find(x=>x.id===id);if(!l){lessons();return}let first=MCQS.findIndex(x=>x[4]===id);app.innerHTML=`<div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="#lessons">Lessons</a> / ${l.number} ${l.title}</div><div class="lesson-hero"><div><span class="pill">CHAPTER ${l.number} · PRINTED pp. ${l.pages}</span><h1 class="lesson-title">${l.icon} ${l.title}</h1><p class="lead">${l.intro}</p><div class="topic-meta"><span class="pill green">OCR 2.1.5</span><span class="pill purple">${l.time} suggested</span>${state.done[id]?'<span class="pill green">✓ Marked complete</span>':''}</div><div class="action-row"><button id="completeLesson" class="btn primary">${state.done[id]?'✓ Studied — undo':'✓ Mark lesson studied'}</button>${makeButton('Try simulation','sims','small')}</div></div><img src="${l.image}" alt="Annotated 3D infographic about ${l.title}" /></div><div class="lesson-layout"><aside class="panel toc"><div class="eyebrow">IN THIS LESSON</div><a href="#" onclick="return false">Learning objectives</a>${l.sections.map((s,i)=>`<a href="#point${i}" onclick="document.getElementById('point${i}').scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'start'});return false">${i+1}. ${s.h}</a>`).join('')}<a href="#" onclick="document.getElementById('quick').scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'start'});return false">Knowledge check</a></aside><div class="lesson-body"><div class="panel"><div class="eyebrow">AFTER THIS LESSON, YOU CAN</div><ul>${l.outcomes.map(t=>`<li>${t}</li>`).join('')}</ul></div>${id==='structure'?`<div class="panel" style="margin-top:18px"><div class="eyebrow">INTERACTIVE ANNOTATED DIAGRAM</div><h2>Explore the fluid mosaic</h2><div class="sim-stage">${bilayerSvg()}</div><div id="partDetail" class="note"><div class="eyebrow">SELECTED STRUCTURE</div><h3>${state.selectedPart}</h3><p>${COMPONENTS[state.selectedPart]}</p></div><div class="topic-meta">${Object.keys(COMPONENTS).map(name=>`<button class="btn small" onclick="selectPart('${name}')">${name}</button>`).join('')}</div></div>`:''}${l.sections.map((s,i)=>`<section id="point${i}" class="panel" style="margin-top:17px;scroll-margin-top:105px"><div class="eyebrow">CONCEPT ${i+1} OF ${l.sections.length}</div><h2>${s.h}</h2><p>${s.body}</p></section>`).join('')}<div class="note warn"><b>Exam trap:</b> ${l.pitfall}</div><div id="quick" class="panel" style="scroll-margin-top:110px"><div class="eyebrow">KNOWLEDGE CHECK</div><h2>Before you move on</h2><p>${MCQS[first][0]}</p>${MCQS[first][1].map((c,i)=>`<button class="match-item" data-quick="${i}" data-correct="${MCQS[first][2]}">${String.fromCharCode(65+i)}. ${c}</button>`).join('')}<div id="quickResult" aria-live="polite"></div></div><div class="panel" style="margin-top:17px"><p><b>Source:</b> Oxford <i>A Level Biology for OCR A</i>, Chapter ${l.number}, printed pp. ${l.pages}. This is an original teaching adaptation of the chapter, not a reproduction of textbook pages.</p><button class="btn primary" id="finishBottom">${state.done[id]?'✓ Studied':'Mark this lesson studied'}</button> ${makeButton('All lessons →','lessons')}</div></div></div>`;
 const toggle=()=>{state.done[id]=!state.done[id];persist();lesson(id);toast(state.done[id]?'Lesson added to your progress':'Lesson marked as not studied')};$('#completeLesson').onclick=toggle;$('#finishBottom').onclick=toggle;$$('[data-quick]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{const good=Number(b.dataset.quick)===Number(b.dataset.correct);$('#quickResult').innerHTML=`<div class="feedback ${good?'':'bad'}">${good?'✓ Correct':'Try again.'} ${MCQS[first][3]}</div>`})}
function stopSim(){if(raf){cancelAnimationFrame(raf);raf=null}parts=[]}
function sims(){app.innerHTML=head('EXPERIMENT ZONE','Interactive membrane simulations','Change one variable at a time. These are visual teaching models, not real laboratory measurements.')+`<div class="sim-nav">${[['diffusion','Diffusion chamber'],['transport','Transport lab'],['osmosis','Osmosis lab'],['beetroot','Beetroot permeability'],['bilayer','Fluid mosaic builder']].map(([id,n])=>`<button class="${state.simTab===id?'active':''}" data-sim="${id}">${n}</button>`).join('')}</div><div id="simContent"></div>`;$$('[data-sim]').forEach(x=>x.onclick=()=>{state.simTab=x.dataset.sim;stopSim();sims()});renderSim()}
function renderSim(){const t=state.simTab;if(t==='diffusion')diffusionSim();if(t==='transport')transportSim();if(t==='osmosis')osmosisSim();if(t==='beetroot')beetSim();if(t==='bilayer')bilayerSim()}
function control(key,label,value,min,max,step=1,unit='',scope='sim'){return `<div class="control"><label for="${scope+key}">${label}<b id="${scope+key}val">${value}${unit}</b></label><input aria-label="${label}" type="range" id="${scope+key}" min="${min}" max="${max}" step="${step}" value="${value}"></div>`}
function diffusionSim(){const d=state.diff;$('#simContent').innerHTML=`<div class="panel"><div class="eyebrow">SIMULATION 01 / 05</div><h2>Diffusion chamber</h2><p>Observe random particle motion and how a concentrated region tends to even out over time. Move the sliders, then reset to compare conditions.</p><div class="sim-stage"><canvas id="diffCanvas" width="960" height="395" style="width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:17px;display:block;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#eaf8fe,#f7edff)"></canvas></div><div class="data-grid"><div class="data-cell"><small>LEFT PARTICLES</small><strong id="leftCount">–</strong></div><div class="data-cell"><small>RIGHT PARTICLES</small><strong id="rightCount">–</strong></div><div class="data-cell"><small>NET DIRECTION</small><strong id="netDir">→</strong></div></div><div class="controls">${control('left','Initial particles left',d.left,10,90,1,'','d')}${control('right','Initial particles right',d.right,0,70,1,'','d')}${control('temp','Temperature (relative)',d.temp,5,70,1,' °C','d')}</div><div class="action-row"><button id="diffPlay" class="btn primary">${d.playing?'Pause':'Play'}</button><button id="diffReset" class="btn">↻ Reset particles</button></div><div class="note"><b>Investigate:</b> Which condition produces faster mixing? Compare the early difference in particle numbers and temperature. <b>At equilibrium:</b> particles still move randomly, but there is no overall net diffusion.</div><p class="sim-note">Illustrative 2D Brownian-motion model; motion speed is exaggerated for visibility and is not a calibrated physical diffusion measurement.</p></div>`;
 ['left','right','temp'].forEach(k=>$('#d'+k).oninput=e=>{d[k]=+e.target.value;$('#d'+k+'val').textContent=d[k]+(k==='temp'?' °C':'');if(k!=='temp')initParticles()});$('#diffPlay').onclick=()=>{d.playing=!d.playing;$('#diffPlay').textContent=d.playing?'Pause':'Play'};$('#diffReset').onclick=initParticles;initParticles();lastFrame=0;function frame(t){if(state.simTab!=='diffusion'||!$('#diffCanvas'))return;let delta=Math.min(2,(t-lastFrame)/16||1);lastFrame=t;if(d.playing)advance(delta);drawParticles();raf=requestAnimationFrame(frame)}raf=requestAnimationFrame(frame);
 function initParticles(){parts=[];let rand=(a,b)=>a+Math.random()*(b-a);for(let i=0;i<d.left;i++)parts.push({x:rand(30,460),y:rand(35,365),vx:rand(-1.4,1.4),vy:rand(-1.4,1.4),c:'#7c65d3'});for(let i=0;i<d.right;i++)parts.push({x:rand(500,930),y:rand(35,365),vx:rand(-1.4,1.4),vy:rand(-1.4,1.4),c:'#229fb5'});drawParticles()}
 function advance(dt){let mul=(.5+d.temp/40)*dt;for(const p of parts){p.vx+=(Math.random()-.5)*.28;p.vy+=(Math.random()-.5)*.28;let v=Math.hypot(p.vx,p.vy)||1;if(v>2.1){p.vx=p.vx/v*2.1;p.vy=p.vy/v*2.1}p.x+=p.vx*mul;p.y+=p.vy*mul;if(p.x<15||p.x>945){p.vx*=-1;p.x=Math.max(15,Math.min(945,p.x))}if(p.y<20||p.y>375){p.vy*=-1;p.y=Math.max(20,Math.min(375,p.y))}}}
 function drawParticles(){const can=$('#diffCanvas');if(!can)return;const ctx=can.getContext('2d');ctx.clearRect(0,0,960,395);const g=ctx.createLinearGradient(0,0,960,395);g.addColorStop(0,'#e2f7fd');g.addColorStop(1,'#f5edff');ctx.fillStyle=g;ctx.fillRect(0,0,960,395);ctx.strokeStyle='#8abdd1';ctx.lineWidth=4;ctx.strokeRect(10,10,940,375);ctx.setLineDash([7,9]);ctx.strokeStyle='#b8d9ec';ctx.beginPath();ctx.moveTo(480,12);ctx.lineTo(480,383);ctx.stroke();ctx.setLineDash([]);ctx.font='bold 20px Arial';ctx.fillStyle='#376f93';ctx.fillText('LEFT',32,39);ctx.fillText('RIGHT',845,39);let l=0;for(let p of parts){if(p.x<480)l++;const g2=ctx.createRadialGradient(p.x-4,p.y-4,1,p.x,p.y,9);g2.addColorStop(0,'#fff');g2.addColorStop(.22,p.c);g2.addColorStop(1,p.c);ctx.beginPath();ctx.arc(p.x,p.y,8,0,Math.PI*2);ctx.fillStyle=g2;ctx.fill()}$('#leftCount').textContent=l;$('#rightCount').textContent=parts.length-l;$('#netDir').textContent=Math.abs(l-(parts.length-l))<=4?'≈ 0':l>parts.length-l?'→':'←'}
}
function transportSim(){const d=state.transport;let passive=d.kind!=='active',left=d.left,right=d.right,dir=left===right?'No net movement':(passive?(left>right?'LEFT → RIGHT':'RIGHT → LEFT'):(left>right?'RIGHT → LEFT':'LEFT → RIGHT'));let possible=passive||d.atp;let works=(d.kind==='simple' ? d.solute==='oxygen' : true);$('#simContent').innerHTML=`<div class="panel"><div class="eyebrow">SIMULATION 02 / 05</div><h2>Transport Lab</h2><p>Compare simple diffusion, facilitated diffusion and ATP-driven active transport. Choose an ion/polar molecule and adjust concentration on each side.</p><div class="tabbar">${[['simple','Simple diffusion'],['facilitated','Facilitated diffusion'],['active','Active transport']].map(([k,n])=>`<button data-kind="${k}" class="${d.kind===k?'active':''}">${n}</button>`).join('')}</div><div class="sim-stage"><svg viewBox="0 0 900 335" aria-label="Membrane transport process schematic"><defs><linearGradient id="tbg" x1="0" x2="1"><stop stop-color="#e6faff"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#f2ebff"/></linearGradient></defs><rect width="900" height="335" rx="16" fill="url(#tbg)"/><text x="40" y="36" font-size="23" font-weight="800" fill="#26738e">SIDE A · ${left}</text><text x="685" y="36" font-size="23" font-weight="800" fill="#6d54a4">SIDE B · ${right}</text><rect x="415" y="17" width="70" height="300" rx="15" fill="#ffe4b9" opacity=".8"/>${Array.from({length:10},(_,i)=>`<circle cx="425" cy="${35+i*27}" r="9" fill="#b5a1ef"/><circle cx="474" cy="${35+i*27}" r="9" fill="#b5a1ef"/><path d="M431 ${42+i*27} L465 ${42+i*27}" stroke="#e2a25b" stroke-width="7"/>`).join('')}${d.kind!=='simple'?`<rect x="420" y="93" width="61" height="150" rx="29" fill="#369fc1" stroke="#1f739c" stroke-width="5"/><path d="M448 105 L448 225" stroke="#bdefff" stroke-width="16" stroke-linecap="round"/>`:''}${Array.from({length:Math.round(left/7)},(_,i)=>`<circle cx="${45+(i%8)*43}" cy="${76+Math.floor(i/8)*47}" r="11" fill="${d.solute==='oxygen'?'#e9868c':'#9178dc'}"/>`).join('')}${Array.from({length:Math.round(right/7)},(_,i)=>`<circle cx="${552+(i%8)*43}" cy="${76+Math.floor(i/8)*47}" r="11" fill="${d.solute==='oxygen'?'#e9868c':'#9178dc'}"/>`).join('')}<text x="450" y="296" text-anchor="middle" font-size="18" fill="#26738e">${d.kind==='simple'?'BILAYER':d.kind==='active'?'ATP PUMP':'CHANNEL / CARRIER'}</text>${possible&&works&&left!==right?`<path d="${dir.startsWith('LEFT')?'M360 155 L540 155':'M540 155 L360 155'}" stroke="#de843d" stroke-width="13" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-dasharray="20 14" class="moving-arrow"/><text x="450" y="65" text-anchor="middle" font-size="20" font-weight="800" fill="#1a7e98">${dir}</text>`:''}</svg></div><div class="controls">${control('left','Side A concentration',left,0,100,1,'','t')}${control('right','Side B concentration',right,0,100,1,'','t')}<div class="control"><label>Substance</label><select id="tSolute" class="glossary-search" style="margin:0;padding:9px"><option value="oxygen" ${d.solute==='oxygen'?'selected':''}>Oxygen (non-polar)</option><option value="glucose" ${d.solute==='glucose'?'selected':''}>Glucose (polar)</option><option value="sodium" ${d.solute==='sodium'?'selected':''}>Sodium ion (Na⁺)</option></select></div></div><label class="inline-check"><input id="atpToggle" type="checkbox" ${d.atp?'checked':''}> ATP available (for active transport)</label><div class="note ${(!works||!possible)?'warn':''}" id="transportExplain"><b>${!works?'No direct passage':!possible?'Pump stopped':left===right?'No gradient':dir}.</b> ${!works?'This solute does not readily cross the hydrophobic bilayer by simple diffusion; use a transport protein.':!possible?'ATP is unavailable, so this ATP-driven pump cannot function.':d.kind==='simple'?'Small non-polar oxygen molecules can diffuse directly down their concentration gradient.':d.kind==='facilitated'?'Facilitated diffusion uses a specific channel or carrier, but no ATP is required; net movement follows the concentration gradient.':'A carrier can pump a solute from the side with lower concentration to the side with higher concentration using ATP.'}</div><p class="sim-note">Direction is schematic; biological transport is specific to the actual protein, cellular conditions and solute. Side A and B are generic, not necessarily inside/outside.</p></div>`;
 $$('[data-kind]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{d.kind=b.dataset.kind;transportSim()});['left','right'].forEach(k=>$('#t'+k).oninput=e=>{d[k]=+e.target.value;transportSim()});$('#atpToggle').onchange=e=>{d.atp=e.target.checked;transportSim()};$('#tSolute').onchange=e=>{d.solute=e.target.value;transportSim()}
}
function osmosisSim(){const d=state.osmosis;let out=-Math.round(d.outside*1000),inside=-400,water=out>inside?'Water enters':out<inside?'Water leaves':'No net movement';let r=out>inside?'in':'out';let high=water==='Water enters',low=water==='Water leaves',plant=d.cell==='plant';let status=plant?(high?'TURGID':low?'PLASMOLYSING':'FLACCID'):(high?'SWELLING / LYSIS RISK':low?'CRENATING':'NORMAL'),cellR=plant?0:high?92:low?59:75;$('#simContent').innerHTML=`<div class="panel"><div class="eyebrow">SIMULATION 03 / 05</div><h2>Osmosis & Cell Response</h2><p>Water moves from higher (less negative) to lower (more negative) water potential through a partially permeable membrane.</p><div class="action-row"><button class="btn ${plant?'primary':''}" data-cell="plant">🌿 Plant cell</button><button class="btn ${!plant?'primary':''}" data-cell="animal">🩸 Animal cell</button></div><div class="sim-stage"><svg viewBox="0 0 900 420" role="img" aria-label="Osmosis simulator showing plant or animal cell in an aqueous solution"><defs><linearGradient id="og" x1="0" x2="1"><stop stop-color="#ebfaff"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#efeaff"/></linearGradient></defs><rect width="900" height="420" rx="18" fill="url(#og)"/><text x="26" y="42" font-size="24" font-weight="800" fill="#26738e">OUTSIDE Ψ = ${out} kPa</text><text x="26" y="77" font-size="20" fill="#517b92">CELL Ψ (model) = −400 kPa</text>${Array.from({length:33},(_,i)=>`<circle cx="${45+(i*79)%810}" cy="${105+(i*61)%275}" r="${4+i%3}" fill="#47b5e0" opacity=".5"/>`).join('')}${plant?`<rect x="314" y="111" width="280" height="270" rx="32" fill="#8dc75f" stroke="#518d35" stroke-width="14"/><rect x="${low?349:327}" y="${low?145:124}" width="${low?205:254}" height="${low?205:244}" rx="24" fill="#f6fff5" stroke="#32aa83" stroke-width="9"/><rect x="${low?372:349}" y="${low?167:146}" width="${low?159:210}" height="${low?158:195}" rx="60" fill="#8fd9f6" stroke="#3aaac8" stroke-width="6" opacity=".94"/>${Array.from({length:6},(_,i)=>`<ellipse cx="${low?370+(i%3)*78:351+(i%3)*95}" cy="${low?158+Math.floor(i/3)*176:145+Math.floor(i/3)*204}" rx="17" ry="10" fill="#5cad63"/>`).join('')}<circle cx="${low?393:386}" cy="${low?329:324}" r="20" fill="#9d7ad6"/>`:`<circle cx="450" cy="243" r="${cellR}" fill="#ef8295" stroke="#c34c6b" stroke-width="${high?2:8}"/><circle cx="450" cy="243" r="${cellR*.5}" fill="#ffb3bd" opacity=".8"/><path d="M${450-cellR*.5} ${243} Q450 ${243-19} ${450+cellR*.5} ${243}" fill="none" stroke="#d56f85" stroke-width="6"/>`}${water!=='No net movement'?`<path d="${high?'M200 243 L300 243 M700 243 L610 243':'M315 243 L207 243 M585 243 L690 243'}" stroke="#238dcb" stroke-width="10" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-dasharray="20 10"/><text x="450" y="402" text-anchor="middle" font-size="23" font-weight="800" fill="#326d8a">${status}</text>`:`<text x="450" y="402" text-anchor="middle" font-size="23" font-weight="800" fill="#326d8a">${status}</text>`}</svg></div><div class="controls">${control('outside','Sucrose outside (model)',d.outside,0,.9,.05,' mol dm⁻³','o')}<div class="data-cell"><small>OUTSIDE WATER POTENTIAL</small><strong>${out} kPa</strong></div><div class="data-cell"><small>NET MOVEMENT</small><strong style="font-size:19px">${water}</strong></div></div><div class="note"><b>${status}:</b> ${high?'Outside water potential is higher (less negative) than inside. Net water enters by osmosis.':low?'Outside water potential is lower (more negative) than inside. Net water leaves by osmosis.':'Water potentials are equal in this simplified model, so there is no net water movement.'} ${plant?(high?'Rigid cell wall resists expansion and turgor pressure increases.':low?'The vacuole/protoplast shrinks away from the cell wall if sufficient water is lost.':'A flaccid cell has limited turgor pressure.'):(high?'Animal cells have no cellulose wall and may lyse.':low?'Red blood cells shrink and can become crenated.':'Cell maintains overall shape.')}</div><p class="sim-note">Important: numerical water potentials in this teaching simulation are an <b>illustrative linear relationship</b>, not measured or a universal sucrose ↔ Ψ conversion. Actual values also depend on temperature and pressure.</p></div>`;$$('[data-cell]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{d.cell=b.dataset.cell;osmosisSim()});$('#ooutside').oninput=e=>{d.outside=+e.target.value;osmosisSim()}}
function beetSim(){let d=state.beet,heat=Math.max(0,(d.temp-28)/62),sol=d.ethanol/70,tim=d.time/40,release=Math.min(1,(heat*heat*.82+sol*.7+heat*sol*.25)*(.5+tim*.5));let intensity=Math.round(release*95),abs=release*1.45;$('#simContent').innerHTML=`<div class="panel"><div class="eyebrow">SIMULATION 04 / 05 · PRACTICAL</div><h2>Beetroot membrane permeability</h2><p>Heat and organic solvents may damage plasma and vacuole membranes, releasing beetroot pigment into water. Adjust conditions to predict leakage.</p><div class="sim-stage"><svg viewBox="0 0 900 355" role="img" aria-label="Beetroot pigment leakage test tube and illustrative absorbance graph"><defs><linearGradient id="glass" x1="0" x2="1"><stop stop-color="#eef9ff" stop-opacity=".75"/><stop offset=".5" stop-color="#fff" stop-opacity=".45"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#e7f3ff" stop-opacity=".8"/></linearGradient></defs><rect width="900" height="355" rx="18" fill="#f3fbff"/><path d="M158 55 V270 Q158 320 206 320 Q254 320 254 270 V55" stroke="#8ac7dc" stroke-width="12" fill="url(#glass)"/><path d="M168 110 V272 Q168 308 206 308 Q244 308 244 272 V110 Z" fill="rgb(${190-intensity},${80-intensity*.55},${125-intensity*.6})" opacity="${.2+release*.75}"/><rect x="177" y="239" width="58" height="20" rx="7" fill="#9b255e" transform="rotate(-8 206 248)"/><text x="206" y="35" text-anchor="middle" font-size="23" font-weight="800" fill="#3a7996">PIGMENT</text><text x="206" y="343" text-anchor="middle" font-size="18" fill="#688fa6">BETALAIN LEAKAGE</text><line x1="405" y1="283" x2="849" y2="283" stroke="#8aa8b9" stroke-width="3"/><line x1="405" y1="73" x2="405" y2="283" stroke="#8aa8b9" stroke-width="3"/><path d="M405 278 Q525 274 600 239 T848 85" stroke="#a756a1" stroke-width="7" fill="none"/><circle cx="${405+(d.temp-5)/85*444}" cy="${283-Math.min(1,(Math.max(0,(d.temp-28)/62)**2*.82+sol*.7)*(.5+tim*.5))*198}" r="13" fill="#e88544" stroke="white" stroke-width="4"/><text x="608" y="323" font-size="20" font-weight="800" fill="#427f99">TEMPERATURE →</text><text x="427" y="57" font-size="18" font-weight="800" fill="#427f99">PIGMENT RELEASE ↑</text><text x="489" y="129" font-size="15" fill="#849bad">Qualitative trend · not real data</text></svg></div><div class="controls">${control('temp','Temperature',d.temp,5,90,1,' °C','b')}${control('ethanol','Ethanol concentration',d.ethanol,0,70,5,' %','b')}${control('time','Exposure time',d.time,5,40,5,' min','b')}</div><div class="data-grid"><div class="data-cell"><small>MODEL ABSORBANCE</small><strong>${abs.toFixed(2)}</strong></div><div class="data-cell"><small>PREDICTED LEAKAGE</small><strong>${release<.2?'Low':release<.55?'Moderate':'High'}</strong></div><div class="data-cell"><small>MEASURE WITH</small><strong style="font-size:18px">Colorimeter</strong></div></div><div class="note"><b>Practical design:</b> identical washed beetroot discs, same source, time, water volume, pH and rinsing, appropriate temperature controls, repeats and means. Use colorimeter absorbance as a proxy for concentration. <b>Do not call model values experimental results.</b></div><p class="sim-note">This is a qualitative simulation. The test-tube colour and numerical absorbance are invented for learning; real thresholds and responses depend on tissue, solvent, temperature and time.</p></div>`;['temp','ethanol','time'].forEach(k=>$('#b'+k).oninput=e=>{d[k]=+e.target.value;beetSim()})}
function bilayerSim(){$('#simContent').innerHTML=`<div class="panel"><div class="eyebrow">SIMULATION 05 / 05</div><h2>Build your fluid mosaic understanding</h2><p>Tap proteins, lipids and surface molecules on the diagram to learn what each does. Study each part, then test yourself with membrane hotspot practice.</p><div class="sim-stage">${bilayerSvg()}</div><div id="partDetail" class="note"><div class="eyebrow">SELECTED COMPONENT</div><h3>${state.selectedPart}</h3><p>${COMPONENTS[state.selectedPart]}</p></div><div class="topic-meta">${Object.keys(COMPONENTS).map(n=>`<button class="btn small" onclick="selectPart('${n}')">${n}</button>`).join('')}</div><div class="action-row">${makeButton('Try hotspot practice →','practice','primary')}</div></div>`}
function practice(){app.innerHTML=head('RETRIEVAL & ACTIVE RECALL','Practice playground','Learn by doing: immediate feedback, guided hints, correct explanations and memory tracking.')+`<div class="tabbar">${[['quiz','Quick quiz (30)'],['bankmcq','Past-paper-style MCQ (30)'],['bankmsq','Multi-select MSQ (30)'],['blanks','Fill the blanks'],['match','Matching'],['hotspot','Hotspot labels'],['sequence','Put in order'],['flash','Flashcards']].map(([k,n])=>`<button class="${state.practiceTab===k?'active':''}" data-ptab="${k}">${n}</button>`).join('')}</div><div id="practiceContent"></div>`;$$('[data-ptab]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{state.practiceTab=b.dataset.ptab;practice()});practiceRender()}
